@startuml
title Governance (OpenAPI/Contracts/SLAs/Deprecation + Service Catalog) - TARGET P3

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "HAP Microservices" as HAP {
  component "auth-service" as Auth
  component "clients-service" as Clients
  component "doctors-service" as Doctors
  component "appointments-service" as Appointments
  component "notes-service" as Notes
}

component "OpenAPI Specs\n(per service)" as OpenAPI
component "Contract Tests\n(Pact)" as Pact
component "Service Catalog\n(Backstage - optional)" as Catalog
component "SLA/SLO Dashboard\n(Grafana/Docs)" as SLA

component "API Consumers\n(frontend/postman/other services)" as Consumers

Consumers --> HAP : call REST APIs (versioned)

Auth --> OpenAPI : generates/maintains spec
Clients --> OpenAPI : generates/maintains spec
Doctors --> OpenAPI : generates/maintains spec
Appointments --> OpenAPI : generates/maintains spec
Notes --> OpenAPI : generates/maintains spec

OpenAPI --> Pact : provider/consumer contracts
Consumers --> Pact : consumer expectations
Pact --> HAP : verification in CI

HAP --> Catalog : metadata (owner, links, docs)\n(optional)
HAP --> SLA : export metrics (latency, errors, uptime)

note right of OpenAPI
Versioning:
- /v1/... and /v2/...
- breaking changes => new version
end note

note right of Consumers
Deprecation Plan:
- anunciar depreciação (Sunset/Deprecation headers)
- manter v1 por X semanas
- guias de migração para v2
- remover após prazo
end note

note bottom of SLA
SLA/SLO exemplos:
- availability 99.9%
- p95 latency < 300ms (GET)
- error rate < 1%
end note

@enduml
